<!DOCTYPE concept PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Concept//EN" "concept.dtd">
<concept id="impala_compute_processing_cost" rev="5.0.0">
  <title>COMPUTE_PROCESSING_COST Query Option</title>
  <titlealts audience="PDF">
    <navtitle>COMPUTE PROCESSING COST</navtitle>
  </titlealts>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <data name="Category" value="Impala"/>
      <data name="Category" value="Impala Query Options"/>
      <data name="Category" value="Performance"/>
      <data name="Category" value="Developers"/>
      <data name="Category" value="Data Analysts"/>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
  <conbody>
    <p>The <codeph>COMPUTE_PROCESSING_COST</codeph> query option determines whether the query
      planner evaluates the CPU processing cost of a query.</p>
    <p>When you enable this query option, the query planner estimates the CPU processing cost of
      each query fragment. The query planner uses this estimate to adjust the degree of parallelism,
      which represents the number of fragment instances scheduled per executor node. This cost-based
      parallelism adjustment improves resource utilization compared to using a fixed degree of
      parallelism.</p>
    <p conref="../shared/impala_common.xml#common/type_boolean"/>
    <p conref="../shared/impala_common.xml#common/default_false"/>
    <p><b>Added in</b>: <keyword keyref="impala43" id="IMPALA-11604"/></p>
    <p conref="../shared/impala_common.xml#common/usage_notes_blurb"/>
  </conbody>
</concept>
